-- `needs` coverage, LET ANNOTATION, COVERED (2026-08-05).
--
-- Accept companion to reject/t151. The identical narrowing under a `needs`
-- that covers it must typecheck.
--
-- `needs IO` against an annotation naming `Cap(IO.FileWrite)` is the point:
-- the new body walk must run its findings through the SAME lattice
-- subsumption that signature caps get, not a string comparison. A module
-- declaring the root capability may narrow to any descendant.
-- Ocap phase 7b retired `Cap(IO.X)` values, so these positions are now shown
-- with a proof capability, which a module must still cover with `needs`. (The
-- lattice-subsumption half no longer applies: proof capabilities are their
-- own roots.)
mod CoveredLetAnn do
  mod Db do
    proof cap Ready
    fn ready() : Cap(Db.Ready) do mint_cap() end
  end
  needs IO.Console
  needs Db.Ready
  fn main() needs IO.Console do
    let r : Cap(Db.Ready) = Db.ready()
    let _ = r
    println("annotated within a declared capability")
  end
end
